<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antĭgŏnē</span></b> ,
			ēs, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antĭgŏna</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀντιγονη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A daughter of the Theban king Œdipus</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hyg.
				Fab. 72</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antigones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					8, 228</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A daughter of the Trojan king Laomedon</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antigonen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					6, 93</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. G. 2,
		320</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
